WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.530
- I don't think there's anything wrong

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.010
with chasing money, I just think that

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.035
it's usually the quickest
way not to get it.

00:00:06.035 --> 00:00:09.370
(calm piano music)

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.300
- [Gary] Did you consider
not going as rogue

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.670
as quitting and going all in?

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.770
Did you consider the practicality of

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.237
6PM to 3 in the morning?

00:00:18.237 --> 00:00:19.500
- [Interviewee] No.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.987
- I'm actually just curious,
there's no judgment,

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:25.818
I'm only collecting data
because I'm fascinated by

00:00:25.818 --> 00:00:29.880
the practicality of it,
and the fear that I have

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.750
when people make ...

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.650
I want everybody to do what you did,

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.060
if they can do it.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.920
And my fear is a lot can't and that

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.860
there's a more practical way than going

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.460
from zero to 100, though
some people have to

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.700
go zero to 100 because if they're

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.120
half pregnant they'll never do it.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.335
It's this completely
interesting matrix, right?

00:00:48.335 --> 00:00:49.168
- [Man] Gary.

00:00:49.168 --> 00:00:50.001
- Please.

00:00:50.001 --> 00:00:50.940
- [Man] They can't or they won't?

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.240
- There's a lot of things going on.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.730
I think first of all, the reason I push

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.670
so much on judgment is the biggest fear

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.902
I have is he won't because

00:00:57.902 --> 00:01:00.925
when I look at them, it's interesting,

00:01:00.925 --> 00:01:03.650
I'm like, "Oh, it's
good," because I wonder

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.400
how much he's driving, hyping him

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.820
to get the team there.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.878
You need optimism and hype to jump.

00:01:11.878 --> 00:01:14.281
Guys, kissing a girl or boy,

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:16.701
riding a bike, going in a pool,

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.870
I've become fascinated
with these three events

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.532
as children, because if you really look

00:01:21.532 --> 00:01:23.940
at it, it's hype.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.657
I remember hyping buddies
in sixth grade be like,

00:01:26.657 --> 00:01:28.405
"Dude you can kiss her."

00:01:28.405 --> 00:01:29.654
Like hype it.

00:01:29.654 --> 00:01:34.482
Or, when looking at friends
or the hype I needed,

00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:36.580
I was scared shitless
to swim or ride a bike,

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.723
hype, like taking a jump.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.300
At the same token, sometimes the dude went

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.880
in for the kiss and she rejected him

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.530
and he was crippled for a decade.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.520
A lot of people will fail in business

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.006
and so I'm unbelievably, you 30 years ago,

00:01:54.006 --> 00:01:56.560
had no choice, you had to jump.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.330
You do have a choice now, depending on

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.163
the business you choose.

00:02:00.163 --> 00:02:02.420
If you open a health and wellness,

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.220
if you open a gym, you've physically

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.053
got to be there.

00:02:06.053 --> 00:02:07.000
You can't.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.730
But if you're doing content or information

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.820
or you could use content to set up

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.978
a grand opening that
will win in three years,

00:02:13.978 --> 00:02:18.653
it's asked literally just for
data of how you got there.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.270
The other thing I'm a very big believer in

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.710
is getting people to not feel like

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.210
it's a scarlet letter if they lose.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.250
Something nobody talks about at all

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.780
is your scenario, you jump,

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:33.400
it fails, you reset and go back,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.000
and get a job in the craft that you had

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.210
because of your resume, and you

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.233
restart in four years from now.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.080
America's pretty good at looking at losses

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.700
in a positive way compared to other parts

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.210
of the world where it's like a true

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.173
scarlet letter death forever.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.240
But still even here, you know, people

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.880
don't know when to go back from their jump

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.830
because they don't want
the loss on the resume.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.930
They made the big to do,
you're doing to do it,

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.030
now it doesn't work,
and what they do is they

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.680
triple down into debt to look good

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.340
in front of people.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.500
- [Woman] What if it did and you never

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.780
jumped to find out?

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.190
- Oh you're preaching.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.270
That I want, you've already done that.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.120
I'm actually talking about the next part,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.820
which is having options to know

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.093
that the game is super long.

00:03:23.093 --> 00:03:26.560
When you go from ice
cold, when you go from

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.200
never having a business
to having a business,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.136
that's like I'm asking you to right now

00:03:32.136 --> 00:03:34.713
qualify for Wimbledon in tennis.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.780
It's a lot harder than people think.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.160
You're grown, you two are grown.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.760
I'm not trying to suppress by the way,

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.560
I'm talking about the
practicality of options.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.460
I love that we live in a world,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.040
I'm trying to get people
to really understand

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.150
how to win this.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.680
So much of my success is
completely predicated on

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.643
not worrying about all my losses.

00:03:57.736 --> 00:03:59.530
which means my great losses are things

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.960
I passed on.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.660
Maybe I should've done Shark Tank.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.380
Maybe, maybe, maybe not.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.570
I don't think I should've done it.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.860
Not this late in, I think
I'll do my own thing.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.930
But, fuck, I mean there's a lot,

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.373
I didn't invest in Uber when
I could've made $400 million.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.310
That's a loss, but all
the things that I've done

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.840
are things that I can't
see what the outcome is.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.360
Let me tell you how
the Uber thing might've

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.490
not been a loss.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.260
On black and white paper,
if I gave Travis the money

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.060
like I always was doing at that time,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.260
I would've made $300,
$400 million on paper.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.230
What if I invested in
Uber and that led me to

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.373
giving a speech in India, based on it,

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.310
and I got hit by a bus and died?

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:54.363
I'm so happy right now,
how could I possibly ...

00:04:55.969 --> 00:04:58.630
You don't know what
life's going to bring you.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.680
Life's complicated, and
way more matrixed out,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.310
and I'm going to start pushing this,

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:04.400
I said it for the first time really

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.960
heavily up there, the ROI,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.233
winning in life is happiness, not money.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.630
What I'm most happy about is

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.363
if you just love the process.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.960
Loving the process,
like loving the debates

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.431
in the kitchen, that's what--

00:05:20.431 --> 00:05:23.580
- [Woman] We're good at
separating that though.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.008
- That's great, I believe
you, your vibes seem good.

00:05:27.008 --> 00:05:29.150
I think that's huge.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.860
To me, it's time and talent.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:34.270
The reason I love hard
work is it's controllable.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.670
It's hard for me to be
like, "Be more talented."

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:47.410
A lot of politically correct over extreme

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.097
European points of view get mad at me:

00:05:50.097 --> 00:05:53.390
"Gary, it's unhealthy,"
"Gary Vee, you can't

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.947
go to the grave with all
your money," and I'm like,

00:05:54.947 --> 00:05:57.282
"Dude I'm not talking about money."

00:05:57.282 --> 00:05:59.803
I don't feel like it's
work when I love it.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.508
Maybe you don't like your job as much.

00:06:03.508 --> 00:06:05.708
- [Woman] Is it wrong
to be driven by money?

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.220
- I don't think I can judge anything,

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.563
I think the question becomes
what the next thing is.

00:06:13.982 --> 00:06:15.458
To me, what?

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:17.270
- [Woman] (music drowns out speaker)

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.640
- Correct, but I also think that people

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.590
confuse the vehicle now.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.691
So, I think people don't often get

00:06:23.691 --> 00:06:26.013
the right vehicle for the destination.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.370
You're right, it's a
vehicle, now my question is

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.810
what's your destination?

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.950
And if you told me it was down the street,

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.500
I'd tell you to fucking walk not

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.953
drive a Lamborghini.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.360
So I don't think it's an evil

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.600
or it's wrong, I think
people are confused to

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:45.140
why they try to amass it, and for what.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.220
How much do you want to make?

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.173
It's arbitrary, what's it based on?

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.260
We have to unwind what's been pushed

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.715
in our heads, you know?

00:06:53.715 --> 00:06:57.171
20, 50, 72, 496, what?

00:06:57.171 --> 00:07:00.010
To me, my big one, is can I do what

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.810
I want to do every day?

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.490
I was doing that running the liquor store

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:04.470
and I was making 57,

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.370
I was happy as fuck.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:10.150
I'm no more happy today than I was at 22.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.120
I was pumped, I was on a mission to build

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.460
a family business so big so that everybody

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.070
on Earth would always say I did the

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.310
right thing by my parents in the way

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.310
they did to me.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.690
I don't think there's anything wrong with

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:24.480
chasing money, I just
think that it's usually

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.030
the quickest way not to get it.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.393
I really believe that, I really do.

00:07:30.393 --> 00:07:33.605
When I watch people that
are driven by money,

00:07:33.605 --> 00:07:37.010
I see a lot of unhappiness and failure.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.120
It's very common.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.281
I think the question is why.

00:07:40.281 --> 00:07:41.600
What do you need?

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.840
And do you have a sense of that?

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.520
Because by the way it evolves.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.290
What he needed at 24
is different than what

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.823
he needs now, and him, and me,

00:07:47.823 --> 00:07:49.620
so it evolves too.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.590
If we did the happy meter here,

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:52.840
it's the people that are,

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.370
I promise you it's the people that are

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.020
doing what they want to be doing.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.110
To me, I couldn't explain to you enough,

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:02.070
and I have utmost empathy for the cynicism

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.950
around this statement, it's unbelievable

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.890
how much I don't like money.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:11.050
I like the game, I love my game.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.340
I love the game of building shit.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.760
It's why building a legacy is the best,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.340
because it's triple
compounding valuable, right?

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.890
I love the admiration.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.350
I talk a lot about loving Rocky 6,

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.110
because he goes back
to not having anything.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:28.950
I talk about it a lot,
it's the same reason

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:31.610
I was selling baseball cards on Saturday.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.190
I was selling baseball cards
on Twitter on Saturday.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:37.250
For $50 for a stack of cards.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:42.250
I love the game of growing, you know?

00:08:42.576 --> 00:08:45.510
To me, the best part is the beginning.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.130
I love the thrill of the chase.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.480
I wake up at six o'clock in the morning

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.830
and go garage sale-ing because there's

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.270
nothing like pulling up,
literally to this day

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.053
I can't replicate the high of going to

00:08:55.053 --> 00:09:00.020
a garage sale, walking
into a yard of junk,

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.610
and finding something for a dollar,

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:04.110
that I know I can sell on eBay for $17,

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.280
is a bigger happiness high than closing

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.980
a $6 million account for Vayner,

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.420
and it's not even close.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.380
That's what I want for everybody,

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.270
because that's how they get the 20.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:16.053
I believe that, I really do.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:19.360
So, I think the fear I have with

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.803
chasing money is it's short term behavior.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.720
And it leads to a lot of negativity,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.850
even for the people that achieve it.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.987
It's why optimism or offense works,

00:09:30.987 --> 00:09:33.020
you know it does.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.620
But I do think you need to be thoughtful

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.180
about the chasing the money thing,

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.340
it will lead to a loss in the macro,

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.220
I believe that.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.880
I could be wrong, but that is my

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.123
official point of view, and
I've watched it way too much.

